---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: 5 Whys Worksheet
description: "A guided 5 Whys worksheet: move from a symptom to a root cause, agree one countermeasure and print or save the result."
activeNav: /tools.html
permalink: /tools/five-whys/
---
<section class="shell page-hero tool-hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Free tool · Root cause</p>
  <h1>5 Whys</h1>
  <p class="lede">Start from what happened, not from who did it. Ask why until the answer is something you can change in the process, then agree one countermeasure and one owner.</p>
</section>

<section class="shell tool-layout">
  <form class="tool-panel worksheet" data-worksheet>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="ws-problem">Problem</label>
      <textarea id="ws-problem" name="problem" rows="3" placeholder="What happened, where, when and how often? e.g. 14 late check-outs last week on the evening shift" data-store></textarea>
    </div>

    <ol class="why-list" data-whys>
      {%- for i in range(1, 6) %}
      <li class="field why">
        <label for="ws-why-{{ i }}">Why {{ i }}?</label>
        <input id="ws-why-{{ i }}" name="why{{ i }}" autocomplete="off" data-store>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
    <button class="button-ghost" type="button" data-add-why>+ Add another why</button>

    <div class="worksheet-grid">
      <div class="field wide">
        <label for="ws-cause">Root cause</label>
        <textarea id="ws-cause" name="cause" rows="2" placeholder="The last answer that you can act on" data-store></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="field wide">
        <label for="ws-action">Countermeasure</label>
        <textarea id="ws-action" name="action" rows="2" placeholder="One change to the process, not a reminder" data-store></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="ws-owner">Owner</label>
        <input id="ws-owner" name="owner" autocomplete="off" data-store>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="ws-due">Due date</label>
        <input id="ws-due" name="due" type="date" data-store>
      </div>
      <div class="field wide">
        <label for="ws-check">How will you know it worked?</label>
        <input id="ws-check" name="check" placeholder="e.g. Late check-outs below 3 per week for four weeks" autocomplete="off" data-store>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-actions">
      <button class="button-primary" type="button" data-print>Print or save as PDF</button>
      <button class="button-secondary" type="button" data-copy>Copy as text</button>
      <button class="button-secondary" type="button" data-clear>Clear</button>
    </div>
    <p class="form-note" data-status aria-live="polite">Your draft is kept only in this browser.</p>
  </form>

  <aside class="tool-aside">
    <p class="kicker">Good whys</p>
    <ul class="tips">
      <li><strong>Facts, not guesses.</strong> Go and look before you answer.</li>
      <li><strong>Process, not people.</strong> "Anna forgot" is not a root cause. Why was it possible to forget?</li>
      <li><strong>Stop at something you can change.</strong> Sometimes that is at why 3, sometimes at why 7.</li>
      <li><strong>Test it backwards.</strong> Read from the root cause up with "therefore". If the chain holds, you are close.</li>
      <li><strong>A reminder is not a fix.</strong> If the countermeasure is "tell people again", ask one more why.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="privacy-note">Nothing you write is sent anywhere. It stays on this device until you clear it.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

<script src="/js/five-whys.js" defer></script>
